                "service_icon": "https:\/\/static.licdn.com\/aero-v1\/sc\/h\/al2o9zrvru7aqj8e1x2rzsrca",
                "id": 1,
                "original_url": "https:\/\/www.linkedin.com\/posts\/eernoult_everyone-is-obsessing-over-geo-right-now-share-7430189189175963648-JUGS\/?utm_source=share&amp;utm_medium=member_desktop&amp;rcm=ACoAAACgR0AB6SQZY5-F9k_waRhMjGlUlk-ZV9I",
                "fallback": "Everyone is obsessing over GEO right now. But most marketers are missing the same thing they missed 10 years ago with SEO: Language :earth_africa:  Context is everything for LLMs.  If you are not optimizing for… | Eugene Ernoult",
                "text": "Everyone is obsessing over GEO right now. But most marketers are missing the same thing they missed 10 years ago with SEO: Language :earth_africa:\n\nContext is everything for LLMs.\n\nIf you are not optimizing for the languages your audience is actually typing into ChatGPT, you are leaving visibility &amp; traffic on the table.\n\nIf someone searches in Spanish, German, or French and your content only exists in English, you are simply not part of the answer.\n\nSo we decided to look at it properly.\n\nI’m teaming up with Erik from Ahrefs and Julien from Getfluence for a deep dive into Multilingual GEO.\n\nWe’ll dig into questions like:\n\n:chart_with_upwards_trend: Does having a multilingual site really improve your overall GEO visibility?\n\n:mag_right: Is ChatGPT really searching the web in other languages, or mostly translating fan out queries and relying on English results?\n\n:rotating_light: How much multilingual traffic is Google quietly intercepting before it reaches you?\n\nNo theory. No recycled SEO takes. Just data and real examples.\n\nLink is in the comments if you want to join!\n\nIf you have any questions about multilingual GEO, drop them below. We’ll make sure to cover them",
                "title": "Everyone is obsessing over GEO right now. But most marketers are missing the same thing they missed 10 years ago with SEO: Language :earth_africa:  Context is everything for LLMs.  If you are not optimizing for… | Eugene Ernoult",
